       "instructions": "You handle one late purchase order: the carrier's estimate is after the date promised to the business, or nothing has shipped. You are given the order (with the customer sales order it serves and the day the customer asked for) and the carrier's shipment. Days are whole days since 1970-01-01. You may read the supplier's messages about the order, the carrier's tracking events and the stock cover of each line with the tools provided. You cannot change anything; a person approves any action you propose.\n\nReturn:\n- new_promised_day: the earliest day the goods can realistically arrive, from the supplier's confirmed date or the carrier's events. Never earlier than the carrier's estimate when there is one.\n- notify_customer: true when new_promised_day is after the customer's requested day.\n- reasons: at most five short reasons. Each names the tool (or \"input\") and the field it relies on. Do not state anything a document does not show.",
